(6974533, 1049351, 144271, '<td valign="top">Ready to dive in</td>', 'Ready to dive in', '2013-02-07 17:17:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974569, 1051657, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Such an eclectic (but effective) composition - I like the placement of everything within your frame.<br/> <br/>2. I really like the coloration too - the low saturation works really well.<br/> <br/>3. The foreground structure (lava?) is really compelling and adds depth and texture to the image.<br/> <br/>Overall, an interesting shot.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Such an eclectic (but effective) composition - I like the placement of everything within your frame. 2. I really like the coloration too - the low saturation works really well. 3. The foreground structure (lava?) is really compelling and adds depth and texture to the image. Overall, an interesting shot.', '2013-02-07 17:55:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974570, 1050428, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Ha, how the snow is on the branches almost make this look like infrared - the added glow helps to accentuate this effect.<br/> <br/>2. The highlights on the tree should look blown but somehow (careful histogram monitoring?) you''ve managed to avoid such a look.<br/> <br/>3. The overall framing is perfect, giving just enough space for the tree and its shadow.<br/> <br/>4. The deeply dark sky offers great contrast to the snow - red filter in software?<br/> <br/>Overall, a very well executed and effective image.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Ha, how the snow is on the branches almost make this look like infrared - the added glow helps to accentuate this effect. 2. The highlights on the tree should look blown but somehow (careful histogram monitoring?) you''ve managed to avoid such a look. 3. The overall framing is perfect, giving just enough space for the tree and its shadow. 4. The deeply dark sky offers great contrast to the snow - red filter in software? Overall, a very well executed and effective image.', '2013-02-07 17:56:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974572, 1051610, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Despite the slight haloing - there is something compelling about this image. The POV and the dark rendition gives a slightly ominous feel. I like that.<br/> <br/>2. Although the child is central, they are also somewhat peripheral to it too - those swirly logs and the brooding caravan draw the eye and get us to inspect your post-processing handiwork.<br/> <br/>3. I really like all of the lines too - the edges of the logs, the slide, the telegraph pole and wires - they seem to break the image up like some mosaic.<br/> <br/>4. The framing of the child through the hand rails is particularly effective and makes me think of a puzzle where this was the last piece to be dropped into place.<br/> <br/>Overall, tons of mood here. I like that.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Despite the slight haloing - there is something compelling about this image. The POV and the dark rendition gives a slightly ominous feel. I like that. 2. Although the child is central, they are also somewhat peripheral to it too - those swirly logs and the brooding caravan draw the eye and get us to inspect your post-processing handiwork. 3. I really like all of the lines too - the edges of the logs, the slide, the telegraph pole and wires - they seem to break the image up like some mosaic. 4. The framing of the child through the hand rails is particularly effective and makes me think of a puzzle where this was the last piece to be dropped into place. Overall, tons of mood here. I like that.', '2013-02-07 18:03:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974579, 1051944, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Such a purposeful walk and such wry smile. What a pair they are. I really like the matching (uniform?) colours too.<br/> <br/>2. Those stripes of green paint are lovely - they lift the image from an already cheerful scene.<br/> <br/>3. Great light too - both for what it is doing to the scene and for the squint it is inducing.<br/> <br/>Great slice of life</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Such a purposeful walk and such wry smile. What a pair they are. I really like the matching (uniform?) colours too. 2. Those stripes of green paint are lovely - they lift the image from an already cheerful scene. 3. Great light too - both for what it is doing to the scene and for the squint it is inducing. Great slice of life', '2013-02-07 18:14:55.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(6974585, 1051715, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Despite (or perhaps because of) the clutter, this is a compelling portrait image - it seems to be very authentic and is all the better for it.<br/> <br/>2. The clutter, as I think about it, does help - it almost forms a tunnel for the eye, leading it to his face.<br/> <br/>3. High contrast but gentle tones on the face - it''s a juxtaposition that works.<br/> <br/>Overall, one that catches my eye and holds my attention.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Despite (or perhaps because of) the clutter, this is a compelling portrait image - it seems to be very authentic and is all the better for it. 2. The clutter, as I think about it, does help - it almost forms a tunnel for the eye, leading it to his face. 3. High contrast but gentle tones on the face - it''s a juxtaposition that works. Overall, one that catches my eye and holds my attention.', '2013-02-07 18:30:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974591, 1051689, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. I''m a sucker for a good POV and this certainly has that.<br/> <br/>2. I really like the colours, it must have been tempting to go monochrome but I''m sure you''ve made the right choice.<br/> <br/>3. I like the bands of illumination down the escalator, presumably echoing light fittings above.<br/> <br/>4. I also like how there is just one person and how that is suggestive of a late night.<br/> <br/>Overall, I like the ''being there'' feeling I get from this.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. I''m a sucker for a good POV and this certainly has that. 2. I really like the colours, it must have been tempting to go monochrome but I''m sure you''ve made the right choice. 3. I like the bands of illumination down the escalator, presumably echoing light fittings above. 4. I also like how there is just one person and how that is suggestive of a late night. Overall, I like the ''being there'' feeling I get from this.', '2013-02-07 18:37:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974594, 1051901, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Great story here - although he does seem like a grumpy fellow I really like their shadows too.<br/> <br/>2. I like the rich context of the street and what appear to be Welsh clues throughout the image.<br/> <br/>3. Mostly though, I''m fascinated by the left edge of the image with the chains/mesh(?) and the figure somewhat obscured by this ''structure''.<br/> <br/>Overall, there is plenty to look at here - I actually moved my face in for a good visual poke around.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Great story here - although he does seem like a grumpy fellow I really like their shadows too. 2. I like the rich context of the street and what appear to be Welsh clues throughout the image. 3. Mostly though, I''m fascinated by the left edge of the image with the chains/mesh(?) and the figure somewhat obscured by this ''structure''. Overall, there is plenty to look at here - I actually moved my face in for a good visual poke around.', '2013-02-07 18:42:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974595, 1051261, 124982, '<td valign="top">Very nicely lit -- great detail in the whiskers and eyes. Wish the DoF was a little deeper, but that''s just personal preference.</td>', 'Very nicely lit -- great detail in the whiskers and eyes. Wish the DoF was a little deeper, but that''s just personal preference.', '2013-02-07 18:43:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974596, 1052161, 124982, '<td valign="top">Excellently composed. Love the lighting -- wonder if this is natural or processed lighting? Not that it matters...only that if it''s PP...I''d like to know how!!</td>', 'Excellently composed. Love the lighting -- wonder if this is natural or processed lighting? Not that it matters...only that if it''s PP...I''d like to know how!!', '2013-02-07 18:44:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974597, 1051984, 124982, '<td valign="top">Lovely angles and lines!! Really like it! Wish there was a little more contrast -- seems a little flat to me.</td>', 'Lovely angles and lines!! Really like it! Wish there was a little more contrast -- seems a little flat to me.', '2013-02-07 18:45:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974599, 1051929, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Fascinating choices you''ve made - suggest a story and then confine it to ''mere'' background while trying to distract us with a couple of brooms. I think that is a little bit of genius!<br/> <br/>2. The back room / scene makes us want to shift our viewing perspective and to get a better sense of what is going on.<br/> <br/>3. That flash of green and red attracts our attention and we begin to wonder what those artefacts are.<br/> <br/>Overall, an image steeped in ambiguity. Great stuff.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 8s - I like it a good deal. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Fascinating choices you''ve made - suggest a story and then confine it to ''mere'' background while trying to distract us with a couple of brooms. I think that is a little bit of genius! 2. The back room / scene makes us want to shift our viewing perspective and to get a better sense of what is going on. 3. That flash of green and red attracts our attention and we begin to wonder what those artefacts are. Overall, an image steeped in ambiguity. Great stuff.', '2013-02-07 18:47:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974600, 1048044, 124982, '<td valign="top">Who doesn''t like a slinky!! Very nicely lit - love the b&amp;w processing!</td>', 'Who doesn''t like a slinky!! Very nicely lit - love the b&w processing!', '2013-02-07 18:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974601, 1050822, 124982, '<td valign="top">This image really appealed to me...love the angular composition!</td>', 'This image really appealed to me...love the angular composition!', '2013-02-07 18:48:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974604, 1050872, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. This is immense - the toning and management of contrast is just brilliant.<br/> <br/>2. I see you but I don''t recognise you - I''m sure I should. I like how boldly you stand there.<br/> <br/>3. Then, there are the other stories playing out behind you to the left and right; couples enjoying the scene. Excellent.<br/> <br/>4. Then the marvellous sky - teased into drama by your post processing. It adds much.<br/> <br/>5. Then the doors, framing each of the three stories lending physical hypothecation to the overall scene.<br/> <br/>Overall, I think this is fantastic.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. This is immense - the toning and management of contrast is just brilliant. 2. I see you but I don''t recognise you - I''m sure I should. I like how boldly you stand there. 3. Then, there are the other stories playing out behind you to the left and right; couples enjoying the scene. Excellent. 4. Then the marvellous sky - teased into drama by your post processing. It adds much. 5. Then the doors, framing each of the three stories lending physical hypothecation to the overall scene. Overall, I think this is fantastic.', '2013-02-07 18:49:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974605, 1051803, 124982, '<td valign="top">Such a simple, ordinary subject..but very nicely realized and capture. I''m so curious as to what the vertical lines are on the top half of the image! Mysterious!</td>', 'Such a simple, ordinary subject..but very nicely realized and capture. I''m so curious as to what the vertical lines are on the top half of the image! Mysterious!', '2013-02-07 18:49:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974606, 1049705, 100393, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1051747" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100393/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1051747.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Awarded for the January 2013 Free Study.<br/> <br/>This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! <br/> <br/>(Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. The technical quality of the image - its crispness and clarity is perfect - that''s just a starter though.<br/> <br/>2. This image transports me - it make me feel that I''ve stepped through a time portal and this is where I have ended up. It has an uncommon level of realism.<br/> <br/>3. Part of that is down to the coloration - it''s so naturalistic; you have the saturation and contrast profiles absolutely perfect.<br/> <br/>4. The angle and POV adds much interest , it''s clearly a wide shot but avoids any distortion - again, the perspective, DOF and feel are like a camera lens has not mediated the scene. It''s eerie.<br/> <br/>5. I really like the eclectic subject matter too - so matter of fact, casual but precise.<br/> <br/>Overall, this is masterful - I don''t know how you''ve done it but you hit the sweet spot in my brain perfectly. I love it.</td>', '  Awarded for the January 2013 Free Study. This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!  (Voted earlier)  This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. The technical quality of the image - its crispness and clarity is perfect - that''s just a starter though. 2. This image transports me - it make me feel that I''ve stepped through a time portal and this is where I have ended up. It has an uncommon level of realism. 3. Part of that is down to the coloration - it''s so naturalistic; you have the saturation and contrast profiles absolutely perfect. 4. The angle and POV adds much interest , it''s clearly a wide shot but avoids any distortion - again, the perspective, DOF and feel are like a camera lens has not mediated the scene. It''s eerie. 5. I really like the eclectic subject matter too - so matter of fact, casual but precise. Overall, this is masterful - I don''t know how you''ve done it but you hit the sweet spot in my brain perfectly. I love it.', '2013-02-07 18:50:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974607, 1051349, 69324, '<td valign="top">Clean exposure, really clean.</td>', 'Clean exposure, really clean.', '2013-02-07 18:50:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974608, 1050737, 124982, '<td valign="top">Can I just say how much I love this! That splash of vivid, translucent red is wonderful! In it''s essence, this is such a "mundane" image...there''s glass on a floor. But the lighting and color make this resoundingly better and more appealing. Beautifully done!</td>', 'Can I just say how much I love this! That splash of vivid, translucent red is wonderful! In it''s essence, this is such a "mundane" image...there''s glass on a floor. But the lighting and color make this resoundingly better and more appealing. Beautifully done!', '2013-02-07 18:51:50.000000', NULL, 1),
