(6974718, 1052055, 60495, '<td valign="top">As far as a photo you have captured a special moment which is awesome. I only wish the focus would have been on the babies face, when I look at the shot the machines are the sharpest when to me either Mom or the baby should be, and given the title I would expect the baby to be the main focus, still a very precious moment, congratulations!</td>', 'As far as a photo you have captured a special moment which is awesome. I only wish the focus would have been on the babies face, when I look at the shot the machines are the sharpest when to me either Mom or the baby should be, and given the title I would expect the baby to be the main focus, still a very precious moment, congratulations!', '2013-02-07 19:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974727, 1051756, 60495, '<td valign="top">I am sorry but this one just does not work for me, it has a pretty cool sugar sculpture thingy but as far as a photo it really looks to much like someone at a Denny''s restaurant taking a shot of their food to share with friends on some social media site like Facebook. The color difference between table top and the plate is a big distraction which takes away from the sugar sculpture shape being the focal point of the shot.</td>', 'I am sorry but this one just does not work for me, it has a pretty cool sugar sculpture thingy but as far as a photo it really looks to much like someone at a Denny''s restaurant taking a shot of their food to share with friends on some social media site like Facebook. The color difference between table top and the plate is a big distraction which takes away from the sugar sculpture shape being the focal point of the shot.', '2013-02-07 20:07:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974744, 1048693, 60495, '<td valign="top">Wow, they have 8 legs... Oh wait there is a second one hiding! Sorry to be so sarcastic but in wildlife photography having merged animals is a big no no, I think we all fall in love with captured shots of animals that we take because we just get excited to have seen and gotten a shot of a particular animal but any time there are extra legs and horns sticking out it really degrades the image. Still a fun shot but really ends up being a more of a memory shot for the photog but usually not going to be as appealing to others. 4</td>', 'Wow, they have 8 legs... Oh wait there is a second one hiding! Sorry to be so sarcastic but in wildlife photography having merged animals is a big no no, I think we all fall in love with captured shots of animals that we take because we just get excited to have seen and gotten a shot of a particular animal but any time there are extra legs and horns sticking out it really degrades the image. Still a fun shot but really ends up being a more of a memory shot for the photog but usually not going to be as appealing to others. 4', '2013-02-07 20:30:27.000000', NULL, 1),
